{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Behold the children of Israel.</b> According to the plain sense: 'they did not listen to me.' And if you ask: but they refrained from listening because of shortness of spirit etc., therefore he needed to say 'and I am of uncircumcised lips.' Alternatively, perhaps Moses did not know what the verse stated, 'because of shortness of spirit etc.' And I heard from Rabbi Yosef of Lisbon who explained the *kal va-chomer* that Rashi explained — that is: 'Behold the children of Israel' etc. — even because of the shortness of spirit upon them, and I say to them that I come from the Holy One, blessed be He, to redeem you from the bondage — and a person who is in prison and hears that someone has come to redeem him goes out and rejoices to meet him and listens to his voice, yet they did not incline their ear to listen to me — all the more so Pharaoh, for whom I come to abolish his enslavement, will not listen to me.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:47.559754719Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}